meta {
  name: 04_RevokeAdministratorValidation
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  Scenario: Revoking an administrator validates the user

    When the user is an unknown party uuid the request fails
    When the user is an organisation the request fails
    When the user parameter is missing the request fails
    When the user parameter is not a uuid the request fails
    When the user is a person who is not an administrator the revoke succeeds without change

    The service checks the user against the connection rules, so its validation errors point
    at QUERY/to, not at the user parameter.
}
